    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string, GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE) response property with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1 / max 3), documenting that level 4 is reserved for tenure. This drives the generated `OwnerDto`, which now exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer has `membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier(Owner)` derivation and its `@Mapping` with `membershipLevel(Owner)`: start at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3.\n\nOn the audit line: the spec says \"anything that recorded the tier (such as the create audit line) must record the level instead.\" In this codebase the create audit line records only `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` \u2014 it never recorded the tier \u2014 so there was nothing to convert there.\n\n**Test results:** The full suite (`./mvnw test`) is green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`. The new `coreNumericLevel` acceptance test (owner with an email and a unique name \u2192 level `1 + email + namesake0`, capped at 3) passes.",
